    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive engine is centered around **Isaac Paredes** (72.13) and **Mickey Moniak** (69.76), both of whom benefit from highly favorable matchups against back-end rotation arms. **Isaac Paredes** is our strongest play; he faces George Klassen, whose 6.12 xERA creates a massive +19% SP skill advantage. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** projects as an elite start despite a moderate rain risk (37%), largely due to a +14% park factor that boosts his power ceiling. **Corbin Carroll** (66.31) remains a high-floor anchor; his ability to exploit Ranger Suarez\u2019s slow delivery keeps him in elite territory, as we are prioritizing his stolen base upside to mitigate the scarcity in our 5x5 format.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Josh Naylor** (44.49), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Travis Bazzana**. While **Josh Naylor** provides reliable production, the optimizer penalized him heavily (-19%) for the matchup against Kyle Harrison, an elite southpaw who suppresses production significantly more than the opposition facing **Travis Bazzana**. We are also monitoring **Austin Riley** (59.52), who offers a sneaky profile today; despite batting in the bottom third of the order, he benefits from a rare combination of park factors and the base-stealing potential inherent in facing Zebby Matthews. \n\nFinally, managers should note that while **Seiya Suzuki** (64.56) is a strong play thanks to favorable winds and a prime #2 order slot, his status remains dependent on confirming the lineup. We are avoiding the temptation to play **Zach McKinstry** (36.38) or **Cole Young** (38.25), as both fall below our threshold for starting efficiency given the SP skill of their respective opponents. With **James Wood** remaining on the IL, we continue to rely on the depth provided by **Vinnie Pasquantino**\u2014who holds a strong 63.00 score\u2014to provide stability alongside the speed-first contributions of **Jose Caballero** and **Brice Turang**. We will continue to evaluate **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Henry Bolte**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Dalton Rushing**, and **Edwin Arroyo** as the official lineups are finalized.",
